    },
    "Whether a crop changes the physical scale of grain and halation. Off — the default, and the physically true answer — a crop shows less of the same negative, so when it fills the picture its grain is enlarged with it. On, the cropped rectangle is the frame: the Film Format describes the crop, so however tight the crop, it has the grain and halation of a whole frame of that size. It applies as you crop, and switching it develops the open picture again. The film's size tops out at 200 mm, which a crop to about a fifth of a 135 frame's long edge reaches. Not under a film edge, where the crop places the picture in the gate." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "开启后，裁剪会改变颗粒与光晕的尺度，并重新冲洗当前照片。片边开启时无效。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "開啟後，裁切會改變顆粒與光暈的尺度，並重新沖洗目前照片。啟用片邊時不適用。"
          }
        },
        "ja" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "オンにすると、切り取りで粒状感とハレーションの大きさが変わり、現在の写真を再現像します。フィルムの縁がある場合は適用されません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
